{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.AtomKnotMassDerivationProof","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.AtomKnotMassDerivationProof","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.atom_knot_mass_derivation_proof","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.atom_knot_mass_derivation_proof","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L114-L126","doc":"**The full proof of `prop:atom-knot-mass-derivation`.**\n\nThe end-to-end claim is the conjunction of the two derivation legs:\nthe categorical leg (finite-sum Markov trace) and the Archimedean\nrealization (MeV mass).  The post-Archimedean naming is *optional*\n(not part of the derivation) and is therefore not a conjunct.\n\nNamed as a `Prop` over the realization datum (pattern C): the\npipeline `T_w ↦ tr_M(T_w) ∈ ℚ(q) ↦ B(𝔥) ∈ ℝ` holds.  A proof\nawaits the categorical + Archimedean-functor infrastructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.post_archimedean_naming_borrowed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.post_archimedean_naming_borrowed","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L98-L112","doc":"**Post-Archimedean naming (BORROWED, optional, NOT in derivation).**\n\nFor hyperbolic `K = ^T_w`, conventional 3-manifold theory names\n`B(𝔥)/(ρ · m_e)` as `Vol_hyp(K)`, justified post-Archimedean by the\nvolume conjecture [kashaev1997], [murakami-murakami2001], Mostow\nrigidity [mostow1968], and the Gromov norm [gromov1982],\n[thurston1978].  All three are borrowed theorems on the\npost-functor side; none is used in the QOU mass derivation.\n\nNamed as the `Prop` asserting the naming identity\n`volName · (ρ · m_e) = B` (pattern C); the borrowed-theorem content\nis the optional input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.archimedean_realization_to_mev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.archimedean_realization_to_mev","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L86-L96","doc":"**Archimedean realization ℚ(q) → ℝ at `q = q_0`.**\n\n`M(𝔥) = ρ · tr_M(T_w) ∈ ℚ(q)`, then\n`B(𝔥) := m_e · ρ · ι(tr_M(T_w))|_{q = q_0} ∈ ℝ` (MeV).\n\nNamed as the `Prop` relating the realised mass `B` to the\nelectron scale, the SDP multiplicity, and the realified trace\n(pattern C).  Ref: [leitner2026] prop:archimedean-realization-functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.B","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The realised mass `B(𝔥) ∈ ℝ` (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.traceAtQ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.traceAtQ0","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The Archimedean realization `ι(tr_M(T_w))|_{q = q_0} ∈ ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.m_e","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Electron mass scale `m_e` (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.ρ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.ρ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L78-L78","doc":"`ρ` is positive (`ρ ∈ ℕ_{>0}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.ρ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.ρ","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L76-L76","doc":"SDP multiplicity `ρ` of `T_w`'s solution in Wedderburn. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.leg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.leg","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The categorical leg producing `tr_M(T_w) ∈ ℚ(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ArchimedeanRealization","kind":"structure","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L68-L84","doc":"Archimedean realization datum: the categorical leg, the SDP\nmultiplicity `ρ ∈ ℕ_{>0}`, the electron mass scale `m_e`, the\nrealified trace value `traceAtQ0 = ι(traceVal)|_{q = q_0} ∈ ℝ`, and\nthe resulting mass `B ∈ ℝ` in MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.categorical_leg_to_markov_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.categorical_leg_to_markov_trace","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L50-L66","doc":"**Categorical leg → finite-sum Markov trace.**\n\nFrom the GB-filtered structure of `T_w`, the GB spectral sequence\ncollapses at `E_2` (Hecke quadratic), so the `E_∞` page is the\nWedderburn decomposition and the Markov trace is the finite\nFrobenius pairing `tr_M(T_w) = Σ_λ y_λ(q) χ_λ(T_w)`.\n\nNamed here as the `Prop` asserting that the leg's `traceVal` equals\nthis finite sum (pattern C); the structural derivation\n(Yekutieli finite slice + `E_2` collapse + Wenzl + `q`-MN) is the\nopen categorical input.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] prop:gb-spectral-sequence +\n     prop:spectral-sequence-collapse +\n     prop:e-infinity-page-identifications. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.traceVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.traceVal","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The Markov trace value `tr_M(T_w) ∈ ℚ(q)` at the slice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.χ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.χ","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L46-L46","doc":"`q`-Murnaghan–Nakayama characters `χ_λ(T_w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.y","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Wenzl weights `y_λ(q)` (rational at the substrate slice). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.blocks","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Number of Wedderburn blocks (partitions `λ ⊢ n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CategoricalLeg","kind":"structure","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/atom-knot-mass-derivation-proof.lean#L36-L48","doc":"Categorical pipeline datum for a canonical word `T_w`: the\nWedderburn block index set `Λ`, the Wenzl weights `y_λ ∈ ℚ`, the\n`q`-Murnaghan–Nakayama characters `χ_λ ∈ ℚ`, and the resulting\nMarkov-trace value `traceVal ∈ ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}